**Buddy:** :mention[@buddy] · **Manager:** :mention[@manager] · **Help:** #team-help

:::tip Start here
Read this guide on day one and work through it in order. Ask your buddy anything, however small.
:::

## Day 1: access and setup

- [ ] Accounts: email, chat, code host, issue tracker @new-hire
- [ ] Development environment set up with the steps below @new-hire
- [ ] Intro call with your buddy @buddy

:::steps
1. **Clone** the main repository.
2. **Install** the dependencies.
3. **Run** the tests to confirm your setup works.
:::

```bash title="setup"
git clone https://example.com/org/repo.git
cd repo
make setup test
```

## Week 1: first contribution

- [ ] Read the architecture overview @new-hire
- [ ] Ship a small fix from the starter issues @new-hire :due[{{today}}]
- [ ] Shadow an on-call shift @new-hire

## First 90 days

:::timeline
- [ ] **Day 30** — Owns small features end to end
- [ ] **Day 60** — Reviews pull requests for the team
- [ ] **Day 90** — Joins the on-call rotation
:::

